    "body": "## Scope\nChat04.4 wave 1 only: standalone synthetic battle-card preview and deterministic tests. Five new files under `tools/`; no runtime integration, no source/deployed mirrors, no shared renderer, no Chat03/04.1/05 edits.\n\n## Fixture behavior\n- Four chess-style attack/defense entries; separate tactic/color per attack and defense; ready-phrase rotation; inline editing with cancel/confirm and empty fallback; committed moves read-only.\n- Synthetic dual-commit reveal shows four lines together and the pre-supplied mechanical outcome/explanation; never computes gameplay outcomes or votes.\n- Participant/spectator projection (`projectBattle`) hides opponent details before reveal, and gives spectators public-only data; the in-page synthetic data and view toggle are **not** network security.\n- Stable battle IDs shared between feed and disputes; multiple cards, `Ваш ход` counter, expanded state, test-only draft persistence across reload.\n\n## Verification (local, against byte-identical source files)\n- `node --test tools/test_chat04_4_battle_cards.mjs`: **21/21 PASS**.\n- `node --check` for both `.mjs` files: PASS.\n- Original fixture preview was exercised at desktop and mobile browser sizes (not physical Safari).\n- Each of the five published GitHub file contents compared byte-for-byte to the locally checked fixture files: identical.\n- `main@31b7a077820914e92de81239e5ab4099e3dfa558`, draft branch HEAD `eb7e549827923ba1958665ac48626aec130fdf53`; exactly five new `tools/` files, 5 commits ahead, zero behind.\n\n## Acceptance boundaries / next gate\n`ISOLATED_FIXTURE_PASS` only; **NO** in-game, real-user privacy, remote cross-view/reload, server authority, Chat05 vote or Safari runtime PASS. Real spectator data must be server-filtered before delivery. Keep Draft. Independent exact-HEAD review + runtime integration only after approved Chat04.1 source and Chat03 viewer contract; Chat05 vote runtime remains a separate dependency for Chat04.5. No merge, deploy, Cloudflare or Stage7.15.",
